<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ranavalona II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1829">1829</a>–<a href="/years/1883">1883</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ranavalona II was queen of the Merina kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a> from 1868 to 1883. Married to the prime minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rainilaiarivony">Rainilaiarivony</a>, who held real power, she was baptised a Protestant in 1869, after which the royal idols were burned and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> spread rapidly among the Merina. Her reign saw reforms of the law and schools before the first Franco-Malagasy War.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ranavalona-ii.jpg" alt="Ranavalona II" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ranavalona_II,_photograph,_standing.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After the brief reign of Radama II, killed in 1863, real power passed to the prime minister Rainilaiarivony, who held office from 1864 to 1895 and married three successive queens, Rasoherina, <b>Ranavalona II</b> and Ranavalona III.</blockquote><a href="/empire/merina-kingdom">Merina Kingdom · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Ambatomanoina, in what is now <a href="/countries/madagascar">Madagascar</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antananarivo">Antananarivo</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/madagascar">Madagascar</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=-18.32,47.62&amp;year=1864" aria-label="Ambatomanoina on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5841 2843 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Ranavalona II"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6291 3113h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6291 3113h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=-18.32,47.62&amp;year=1864">What was here in 1864? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
